Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Madelyn Lew  M D  Signed Out by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  CLINICAL DATA  53 year old female with a history of right breast cancer  status post lumpectomy on REMOVED_DATE  followed by re excision with positive margins  now here for simple mastectomy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  SKIN  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  SKIN WITH CICATRIX  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh and labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE kg  22 x 19 x 3 4cm mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the axillary tail  There is an exposed lumpectomy cavity just inferior to the areola at 5 o clock  measuring 1 8cm in length  1 3cm in width  and 4cm in depth  The anterior of the specimen is inked in blue  the posterior is inked in black  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a 4 x 2 x 1 5cm cavity lined by tan pink granular and hemorrhagic tissue  The cavity abuts the anterior margin and measures 0 9cm from the posterior margin  Just adjacent to this biopsy cavity and extending superiorly  medially and laterally  is a diffusely tan white fibrotic region measuring 6 x 5 x 3 5cm  The remainder of the parenchyma is yellow tan  lobulated and otherwise unremarkable with no other identifiable masses or lesions  The axillary tail was examined and no lymph nodes were identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma to fibrotic  Received in formalin  and labeled  right breast additional tissue   are 4 fragments of skin covered soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The largest fragment is notable for a nodular surface of the overlying skin  The specimen are all serially sectioned to reveal a homogenous white tan firm cut surface with no obvious mass  hemorrhage or calcifications  Representative sections from each of the 4 fragments in ascending order of size are submitted from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 55 23PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Right Additional   Excision  report_end  , Not Done.
