unostains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show that there is no evidence of vascular invasion  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 25 x 21 x 5cm unoriented modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a 10 x 7 x 3cm axillary tail  which is used to orient the upper outer quadrant  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm disc of skin on the anterior surface  containing an unremarkable nipple and areola  The remainder of the anterior surface of the specimen consists of unremarkable yellow lobulated breast tissue  The posterior margin of the specimen consists of smooth fascia overlying unremarkable yellow lobulated breast tissue  The margins are inked blue anteriorly and black posteriorly  and the specimen is serially sectioned through the posterior margin  There is an ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm stellate area of fibrosis in the upper outer quadrant  adjacent to the axillary tail and 2cm from the posterior and 3cm from the anterior margins  The remainder of the breast proper consists of primarily adipose breast tissue peripherally and primarily fibrous breast tissue centrally  with no additional focal lesions detected  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contiguous section  including stellate lesion and closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contiguous section  including stellate lesion and anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of fibrous tissue in the area of stellate lesion in the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue in inferior lateral quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of superior medial quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from superior medial quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative tissue from central region of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 bivalved axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two attached  serially sectioned lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fat from axillary tail  with possible lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  skin   are 3 portions of unremarkable tan skin  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  Sectioning reveals unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 24   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 20 03PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong co