osterior margins  The cavity comes to within 0 3cm of the anterior margin and within 0 5cm of the posterior margin  The remainder of the breast is tan white  slightly granular  fibrous tissue and a small amount of yellow tan fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  Cavity with nearest relations to anterior and posterior margins  D  Additional section of superior portion of cavity  E  Representative fibrous tissue from lateral breast  F  Representative fibrous tissue with tan cyst from medial aspect  G  Possible lymph nodes from upper outer quadrant  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left chest old incision   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 2 0cm   with a faint linear possible scar at the center  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes H J  with the tips in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  scar plaque  left breast 5 o clock  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of tan white fibrous tissue and small quantities of fatty tissue  which is submitted in toto as cassette K  Resident  PAUL N  STAATS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN LEFT CHEST  RE EXCISION PART C  SCAR LEFT BREAST PLAQUE   5 00  EXCISION , Positive.
