Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 10 55 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ  near margins of prior excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING ABUNDANT CALCIFICATIONS  WITH FOCAL FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS OF SKIN  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN   UNORIENTED EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR   UNORIENTED EXCISION  SKELETAL MUSCLE AND ADIPOSE TISSUE  WITH FOCAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left simple mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left simple mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail and an REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm overlying elliptical eccentrically located tan white portion of skin  There is a short suture designating the axillary tail and a long stitch designating the lateral skin margin  There is an eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple areola complex with a 2 0cm well healed retracted linear scar located 2 0cm lateral to the nipple and 0 5cm from the lateral skin margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm slightly raised  well delineated tan brown slightly granular papule located 1 0cm superior to the nipple and coming to 0 5cm from the superior skin margin  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  The posterior aspect displays a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan pink retracted area  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm well delineated irregular tan pink fibrotic  scarred area and abuts the retracted posterior aspect  and the overlying scar bearing skin  This area contains dense  lobulated fibrous tissue with no discrete masses or lesions grossly appreciated  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink and lobulated  Within the axillary tail  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A J  Entire fibrotic scarred area with the deep closest overlying posterior margin in cassettes A D  and the section containing the metal clip in cassette E  K L  Uninvolved fibrotic lobulated parenchyma  M  Skin papule  N P  Representative sections from axillary tail  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior breast tissue  left   are two irregular tan pink unoriented lobulated portions of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The unoriented specimens are inked black  serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable tan yellow to pink cut surface  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes Q T with the smaller portion in cassettes Q R and the larger portion in cassettes S T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  The unoriented specimen displays a moderate amount of cauterizing artifact along one aspect  and entirely submitted in cassettes U V  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  SAM S  YOO