Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 33 CLINICAL DATA  43 year old female with a history of invasive ductal carcinoma with positive lymph nodes  Status post neo adjuvant chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 17 LYMPH NODES WITH EXTENSIVE EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  SEE TABLE 1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  3  Number of lymph nodes examined  17  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  3  Size of largest lymph node  0 18cm  Extracapsular extension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  Tumor present in soft tissue  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE 2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 2cm from the lateral  medial and inferior margin of the specimen  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the lateral  medial and inferior margin of the specimen  Stains for receptors  Not indicated  NOTE  The prior biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   was reviewed for comparison  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA PRESENT AS A REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block I   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a heterogenous yellow and white cut surface  Approximately 17 lymph nodes are located  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The nodes are submitted in their entirely in cassettes A C  The largest four lymph nodes are bisected and submitted  half of each are submitted in cassettes D and E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm lumpectomy specimen  The superior margin is inked blue  the inferior surface is inked black  the lateral surface is inked yellow and the medial surface is inked green  Serial sectioning reveals a well defined white gray  rubbery nodule  grossly abutting the inferior surface  The mass contains some areas of yellow discoloration  The mass measures in its greatest dimension REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  Representative sections of the mass and its nearest margins are submitted in cassettes F I  Representative sections of breast parenchyma away from the mass are submitted in J and K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast inferior margin   is an non oriented piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue  that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The specimen is sectioned and submitted in cassettes L N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior margin   is a non oriented irregular piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in cassettes O  P  and Q  Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN  EXCISON PART D  BREAST LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION , Not Done.
