Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 15 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   SEE TABLE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI  AGGREGATING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE TABLE  1   METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 6 OF 10 LYMPH NODES   SEE TABLE  2 AND SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Keratin immunostains confirm metastatic carcinoma in the lymph nodes  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple scattered microscopic foci aggregating to  0 3cm  Grade  REMOVED_DATE Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  2  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the posterior and inferior margins of the specimen in two foci  Stains for receptors  Requested on block B  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  6  Number of lymph nodes examined  10  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  4  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 18 30                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy left axillary node dissection   is a 21 x 7 x 2 4cm lumpectomy specimen with attached axilla  There are three guide wires in the specimen and a long stitch marking the lateral and axillary lateral margin and axillary tail  short stitch demarcating the anterior margin  and a bow tie demarcating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal tan yellow adipose tissue with intermixed white fibrous tissue  and numerous palpable nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The nodules are ill defined and in most cases not visually discrete from the surrounding adipose and fibrous tissue  However the largest mentioned nodule is tan pink to tan white and is adjacent to a curled surgical clip  This largest nodule is 0 5cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin 2 5cm from the inferior margin  2 2cm from the superior margin  and greater than 3 0cm from both the medial and lateral margins  The surgical clip is removed and representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Dominant nodule to anterior margin adjacent to curled clip  B C  Additional sections of nodule to anterior margin  D  Nodule to post